sec.p:
Logistic regression models were used to predict CAR-T response at 3 and at 6 months. Three PET parameters (MTVtotal, TLGtotal, and SUVmax), and one radiomics feature (entropy) were selected for assessing CAR-T therapy response at 3 and 6 months. These parameters were selected based on their significant weight in the assessment process. The results indicated an AUC of 0.646, a 20.0% of specificity and 81.5% of sensitivity for the 3-month assessment. For the 6-month assessment, the AUC was 0.718, 90.9% of specificity and 20.0% of sensitivity (Table 3).Table 3
Logistic regression parameters for response prediction at 3-month and 6-month after CAR-T treatment
Response after 3-months of CAR-T therapyResponse after 6-month of CAR-T therapy
