For the assessment of neurotoxicity, logistic regression models able to successfully predict the presence of ICANS (grades 1–4) were developed. A model including four imaging features (MTVtotal, TLGtotal, SUVmax and entropy) achieved an AUC of 0.601, with an 58.5% of accuracy,73.5% of specificity and 41.9% of sensitivity. On the other hand, a model including seven clinical variables — type of CAR-T, cell-of-origin classification, number of lines of received treatment, IPILD score, ECOGLD stage, HCT-CI, and LDHLD ratio —successfully predicted the development of ICANS with better AUC, accuracy, and sensitivity (AUC = 0.830, 71.2% of accuracy, 60.0% of specificity and 82.8% of sensitivity) (Table 5).Table 5
Logistic regression parameters for ICANS prediction after CAR-T treatment
